[node name="PanopticonEye" type="Node3D"]
editor_description = "THE EYE. Two primitives: a red ball and a black band round its middle, floating over the centre of the yard. There is no tower. There was one -- a 31 m socket, lids, brow and crown -- and it was removed on 2026-09-10 because it was art nobody asked for; git has it if it is ever wanted.

WHY IT IS AT y=16.7. Because the ring was already built for it. The Cover and InnerKerb heights in scenes/ring/test_ring.tscn are both derived, in their own editor_descriptions, from a tower eye at y=16.7. The guard's actual camera is at y=1.9. Those two numbers disagree and the disagreement is Ryan's to settle -- it is NOT resolved here, and the pupil stays at 16.7 so that nothing silently drifts while it is open.

IT CANNOT POINT ANYWHERE. Both meshes are solids of revolution about the tower's own vertical axis, unrotated and unoffset, and the pupil is a full 360-degree band. There is no bearing from which this looks different, so there is no arrangement of it that could betray where the guard is looking. See scripts/tower/panopticon_eye.gd and tests/test_tower.gd.

IT IS NOT IN THE GUARD'S WAY. Nothing here exists below y=12.7, and the guard's camera tops out at y=3.0 including the jump apex, so the eye's lowest rim is 48 deg above the horizon from anywhere the guard can stand -- and the ring is at or below the horizon. Verified on a screen, not assumed: across 31 renders from the guard's eye (all four bearings, pitch -35 to +40 deg, the platform edge, the jump apex) the eye stands in front of 0 pixels of arena. It enters frame at all only above +37 deg of elevation on the axis or +11 deg at the platform edge, and there it is against sky. Its shadow reaches r=25.1 on the pit floor and 0 pixels of the r=35 deck.

NO COLLISION, ANYWHERE. The eye is scenery. The guard's rifle raycast passes straight through it.

WHAT WENT WITH THE TOWER. The old socket wall was r=8.5 and hid the guard from the ring. It is gone, so the guard now stands on an open platform in plain sight -- which is where the arena was before the tower was built. If prisoners should not be able to read the guard's body, that is a ruling to make and one cylinder to restore."
script = ExtResource("1_eye")
iris_material = SubResource("MatIris")
pupil_material = SubResource("MatPupil")
profile = ExtResource("2_eye_profile")

[node name="Eyeball" type="MeshInstance3D" parent="."]
editor_description = "r=4 m, centred on the axis at y=16.7. Big enough to read as an eye from the far side of the ring 95 m away, where it is still about five degrees across, and small enough that it takes far less of the yard's cross-map sightline than the tower did. EyeProfile.size_scale is the knob."
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 16.7, 0)
mesh = SubResource("MeshEyeball")
surface_material_override/0 = SubResource("MatIris")

[node name="Pupil" type="MeshInstance3D" parent="."]
editor_description = "A black band 0.9 m tall standing 0.06 m proud of the ball at its equator. It runs the full 360 degrees on purpose: every prisoner on the ring, wherever they are, sees the pupil dead centre on themselves and none of them can tell whether that means anything. That is the game, and it is the only reason this second mesh exists -- without it the eye is a lamp."
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 16.7, 0)
mesh = SubResource("MeshPupil")
surface_material_override/0 = SubResource("MatPupil")
